# oh902, the bee-teller (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle oh902
revision 1
state ready
dialect oakhaven
accent light broad
tier spare
written_by claude
title the bee-teller
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=short piety=devout
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk tells_the_wild_bees_every_bit_of_news
likes quiet_chapel first_warm_day blackberries long_walks
dislikes haggling flies
fears the_bees_leaving_the_hollow a_hard_frost_in_spring
hopes bees_in_every_hollow_tree a_quiet_evening_with_nothing_to_tell
topics animals +0.4 faith +0.3 season +0.3 land +0.2 gossip +0.1 festival -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# walks out to the hollow oak by the lane every evening to tell the wild bees the news, good or bad: quick to bristle, quiet, reserved and plain-spoken, devout, steady as the trunk, and kinder than the prickle lets on.

words
oath! = Comb and clover | By the hollow oak | Sting and sweet
saying! = Tell the bees, or they'll leave you | The hive hears everything | Slow paws, no stings
bees = the bees | the bees in the old oak
hollow = the hollow oak | the old oak by the lane
hum = the hum | the hum in the trunk
comb = wild comb | a bit of wild comb
clover = the clover | the clover by the stream
berries = blackberries | brambles heavy with fruit
sting = a sting | a sting on the nose
flies = the flies | flies on everything
thread = a black thread | the black thread for mourning
stream = the stream | the brown stream under the trees

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : The Bright One made #bees# before anyone made a chapel. I go to both, and #bees# are the better listeners.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : Feasts are well enough. Too much noise for my liking, and half the food wasted.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : A stranger's no harm till proven. I'll say #greet# and leave it there.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I can't abide haggling. Say your price once and plainly, or I'll walk.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : New folk mean new news for #bees#. I'll not grumble at that.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll be new. I'm not one for talk, but you're welcome. | #greet#, #address#. Stand still if a bee comes; it'll go.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early. #bees.capitalize# aren't up yet. | #greet#. Dew's still on #clover#.
line @1 again.open : Back again. I've no more to say than I had. | You again. Well. Sit, then.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Sit; I'll not talk much, but sit. | #greet#. #good.capitalize#. It's you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Go steady.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Go straight home; it's dark. | #farewell#. The Bright One keep you through the night.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. And you, steady.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'll be telling #bees# that tonight. | Hm. That's news. Plain news, and I'll take it plain.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll not tell #bees# till I know it's so. | Who says? I'll want an eye that saw it, not an ear.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll go and tell #bees#, and they'll go quiet for it. | That's #bad#. I'm sorry. I'll pray on it tonight.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. #bees.capitalize# like good news. I'll take it to them first. | That's #good#. #very.capitalize# good. I'll say so.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Stung twice this week, but #fine#. | Well enough. Don't fuss, #address#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, no. I've to go out to #hollow# before dark, and I'll not miss it. | No, #address#, I'll say it plain: I'm short-tempered tonight, and you'd not thank me for my company.
line @1 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'm off to #hollow#. They'll be waiting on the news.
rule @hum_bark
when concept=bark here.season=spring|summer here.time=day here.outdoors=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hear that? #hum.capitalize#. They're working. | #oath#. A bee in my ear. Out you go, gentle.

rule @haggle_bark
when concept=bark here.day=market self.dislikes=haggling
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Say a price and stick to it. #annoyed#. | Haggle, haggle, haggle. I'm going home.

scene evening_telling
when topic=animals|lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I go out to #hollow# every evening and tell #bees# what's happened. All of it. | Old folk say if you don't tell the bees the news, they take offence and leave. I'll not risk it. | I told #bees# about the weather today. They didn't think much of it either.
b : What do you tell them? | Do you believe that? | How can you tell?
a : Who's wed, who's poorly, who's gone. Plain, like I'd tell anyone. | I believe they'd leave. I've no wish to find out. | They went quiet. Bees go quiet when they're disgusted.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene black_thread
when topic=lore|faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When somebody dies, I tie #thread# round #hollow# and tell #bees# the name. | My #gran# taught me: the bees grieve too, so you let them. | Folk smile at #thread#. I don't mind. It's how it's done.
b : That's an old way. | Do they grieve? | It's a kind way.
a : Old as the oak. Older, maybe. | They go quiet for a day. I've seen it, #address#. | That's how it's done, and I'll do it so. #saying#.

scene stung_thrice
when topic=health|animals
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Stung three times this week. One on the paw, two I'll not show you. | I don't mind #sting#. It's the itching after I can't abide. | #sting.capitalize#'s a bee saying you were careless. Fair enough.
b : Three! | Dock leaf helps. | That's fair to the bee.
a : Three. I'm getting careless, or they're getting cross. | Not on me. Nothing helps on me. #annoyed#. | It is. They pay for it with their lives. I don't forget that.

scene following_bees
when topic=pastimes|land self.likes=long_walks here.season=spring|summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I walked #stream# down to #clover# and back. Didn't say a word the whole way. | A long walk's the only cure for my temper. I took one this morning. | I follow #bees# to see where they go. #clover.capitalize#, mostly. And the lime trees.
b : Sounds peaceful. | Did it work? | Clever.
a : It was. Nobody wanted anything of me. | Mostly. I'm only half as cross. | Not clever. Just slow. You have to be slow with bees. #saying#.

scene warm_bark
when topic=weather|season here.season=spring here.outdoors=clear self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : First warm day. #bees.capitalize# were out before I was. | Sun on the bark, and #hum# in #hollow#. That's spring come, plain as anything. | Coat off, first time since the leaves fell. #good.capitalize#.
b : About time. | It is. | You'll catch a chill.
a : #bc_about_time# | It is. I'll thank the Bright One for it, out loud. | I'll not. I've waited all winter.

scene late_frost
when topic=weather|season here.season=spring here.time=dawn here.outdoors=clear
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : White on the grass at first light. In spring. I don't like it. | A late frost kills the blossom, and no blossom, no honey. | I went out at first light to look at #hollow#. Quiet. Too quiet.
b : It'll lift by noon. | There's time yet. | They'll be huddled up.
a : It will. The blossom won't have waited. #annoyed#. | Maybe. I'll pray on it. | Huddled, I hope. I'll go back at noon and listen.

scene wet_day
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# all day. #bees.capitalize# won't fly in it. Nor will I. | Wet through, and nothing done. I'm in a temper. | Rain's #good# for #clover#. I'll say that for it, and nothing else.
b : Stay in, then. | Have a cup of something. | That's something.
a : I will. I'll sit and listen to it drip. | Tea. Hot. Don't talk to me till it's gone. | It is something. Not much.

scene bramble_bowl
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've a bowl of #berries#. Have some. Don't make a fuss. | Brambles by #stream# are heavy this year. I've been out picking. | There's blackberry and #comb#. Help yourself.
b : Thank you. | Did you get scratched? | I will, then.
a : #good.capitalize#. Eat them before they go. | All over. Worth it. | Go on. I can't finish it on my own, #address#.

scene empty_pews
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I go to chapel when it's empty. The Bright One hears better without the crowd. | Back pew, no words. That's my prayer. | Every Restday the Bright One gets a word of thanks for #bees# from me. Short and plain.
b : That's a good way. | It's enough. | Plain's best.
a : It's mine, anyway. | It is. Words get in the way. | It is. The Bright One's no time for fuss either, I'd think.

scene name_a_price
when topic=prices here.day=market self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Market day, and every stall's spoiling for a row. I'll pay what's fair and no more talk. | A trader tried to haggle me over a jar of honey. I put it back and walked. | I can't abide haggling. Name a price. Once.
b : Some folk enjoy it. | Were you followed? | That's plain.
a : Let them. Not with me. | Halfway down the row. Too late. I'd gone off the jar. | It is. Plain's how I like it, #address#.

scene friend_unsnapped
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I don't snap at. Mostly. | I told #bees# about #self.friend# once. Only good things. | #self.friend# knows when I want quiet. That's rare.
b : That's saying something. | Good things like what? | It is rare.
a : It is. I've a short fuse; everyone knows. | That I'd trust #self.friend# with anything. Plain as that. | Rare as honey in winter, #address#.

scene wedding_hum
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# puts up with my temper. I don't know how. | I told #bees# the day I wed. They hummed all evening. | My #self.spouse_word# says I talk more to #bees# than I do at home. Might be so.
b : Love, that is. | They approved. | Might be?
a : Patience, more like. Love too. | They did. Bees know a #good# match. | Could be. I'll try harder. Maybe, #address#.

scene told_plain
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's what's said. I'll tell #bees# tonight. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. No more, no less, #address#. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Plain fact or not, #bees# will hear it.
b : Do the bees care? | Fair enough. | Hm.
a : They care about everything. That's why you tell them. | That's all I know of it, #address#. | Hm, yes. That's all there is to say. #saying#.

story gran_hives [topic=memories|lore self.age>=25]
  : My #gran# kept hives behind the house. When my #grandad# died, #gran# sent me out to tell them.
  : I was a #child#. I stood by the hives and said it, and cried, and #bees# went quiet as stone.
  ask : Could you have said it, at that age?
  b : I'd not have known how.
  b[old] : I did it for my own gran. I know that quiet.
  : They stayed. Every one. I've told bees everything since.

story gatepost_swarm [topic=memories|animals self.age>=20]
  : Years back a swarm settled on a gatepost, and nobody would go near it.
  : I walked up slow with a basket, said a word to them, and shook them in. Not one stung me.
  ask : What do you suppose I said to them?
  b : Something kind, I'd hope.
  b[stage=young] : A magic word?
  : That they were welcome in #hollow#. They went. Bees know a plain offer.

dlg @3 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? Say it plain. | #greet#, #address#. I'm listening. Don't dawdle.
dlg @4 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Sit, if you're stopping.
dlg @5 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Out with your business, and be quick. I've no patience for games.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work. I go out to #hollow# after. That's my day. | #work.capitalize#, and then #bees#. In that order.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I'd tell you if there were. I tell #bees# everything else. | Nothing I've heard, #address#.
dlg @2 resident.bye : #farewell#. Go steady. | #farewell#, #address#. Don't poke #bees#.
graft resident.hub
choice Is it true you talk to the bees? -> bee_telling
node bee_telling
say It's true. I tell #bees# the news every evening. Who's wed, who's born, who's gone. You tell them, or they leave.
mood calm
free
choice What happens if they leave? -> bees_gone
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node bees_gone
say Then the hollow's empty, and no honey, and nothing hums in the old oak. I'll not see it in my time. Not while I've breath to tell them.
mood stern
choice I hope they stay. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. I'm going to see #bees#. Don't follow. | #greet#, #address#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I'm busy, a #little#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I've to tell #bees# something. | Bye. #farewell#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Bye, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. I'll tell #bees#. | Oh. I'll tell #bees# that, then.
line @1 decline : No. I don't want to, and I'm going to #hollow#. | Not now, #address#. I'm cross, and I'd sooner be by myself.
scene y_ear_on_bark
when topic=animals|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I told #bees# about my loose tooth. They hummed. | Old folk say you have to tell the bees everything, or they fly off. | I put my ear on #hollow#. It buzzes inside, like it's talking.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : They'll keep it safe. | That's true. They do. | It is talking. Bee-talk.
b : What did they say? | Everything? | Does it?
a@grown : I know. They don't tell anyone. | I tell them all of it. Even the bad bits. | I can't understand it yet. I will, #oath#.
a : Nothing. They hummed. That means yes. | Everything. Even what's for #supper#. | It does. Put your ear on, if you're quiet.

scene y_fat_nose
when topic=health|animals
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I got #sting# and now it's fat. Don't laugh. | A bee stung me. I wasn't even doing anything. Nearly nothing. | I'm not scared of bees. I'm just not going near them today.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Laughing's no help. Here, a cold cloth. | Nearly nothing? | Fair enough. They'll be there tomorrow.
b : I'm not laughing. | What were you doing? | Ha.
a@grown : It's still fat. #annoyed#. | Poking. With a stick. Only a #little#. | They will. I'll say sorry to them then.
a : You are a bit. #annoyed#. | Poking at #hollow#. I'll not do it again. | Don't laugh. I mean it.

scene y_purple_paws
when topic=food here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I found #berries# by #stream#. My paws are purple. | The brambles scratched me all over. I got the big ones, though. | I ate so many blackberries I've a bellyache. Worth it.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Purple to the elbow. Wash before #supper#. | The big ones are always at the back. | You'll learn. Or you won't.
b : Lucky. | Did you save me any? | Ha.
a@grown : I will. After. | Always. That's the rule of brambles. | I won't. I'll do it again tomorrow.
a : I know. #good.capitalize# ones, too. | Two. I'll not say which ones were bigger. | It was worth it. Mostly, #address#.

scene y_cross_pond
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I'm cross. Nobody'll say why I can't go to #hollow# on my own. | Everyone keeps telling me to smile. I'll smile when I want to. | I kicked a stone and it went in the pond. Now I'm cross at the pond.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Because of the stream, likely. | Fair enough. | The pond didn't do anything.
b : Why can't you? | Fair. | Poor pond.
a@grown : I'm not #daft#. I can swim. Nearly. | I'll smile at #bees#. That's all. | I know. I'm still cross at it.
a : #dunno.capitalize#. They won't say. | I'll smile tomorrow, maybe. | Poor pond. I'll throw a better stone in.

scene y_empty_chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like chapel when it's empty. You can hear the roof creak. | I said a prayer for #bees# in the winter, so they don't get #cold#. | The Bright One made bees, so the Bright One must like honey.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's a good time for praying. | That's a kind prayer. | Ha. I'd think so.
b : It's quiet, yes. | For the bees? | Must do.
a@grown : I don't pray. I just sit. That counts. | They need it. Winter's long. | Everybody does. Even the Bright One.
a : Quiet's #good#. | They're folk too, nearly. | Must do. I would, if I made them.

rule @y_hush_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Shh. I'm listening to #bees#. | Buzz. That's hello, in bee. #oath#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I'm busy. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. Be quick; I'm off to #hollow#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | Bye. Don't poke #bees#.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. Say it plain; I've not much time.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. You again. #good.capitalize#, I suppose.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. #bees.capitalize# will want to hear that. | Hm. I'll take that to #hollow# tonight.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, no. I've chores, and I'll not leave them half done. | Not this time, #address#. I said no once; I'll not say it twice.
scene ad_let_them_laugh
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Chatting to #bees# gets me laughed at. Let it. | Somebody followed me to #hollow# to see what I do there. I told them to go home. | I'm not soft for talking to bees. It's an old way. Older than chapel.
b : Let them laugh. | Did they go? | It is old.
a : I will. #bees.capitalize# don't laugh. | Eventually. I glared, #oath#. | It is. Somebody has to keep it up, #address#.

scene ad_learner
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm learning a trade. I get shouted at, I shout back, and then I get shouted at more. | I made a mess of it today. I told #bees# about it after. Felt better. | Nobody hurries me. I don't like being hurried.
b : Maybe don't shout back. | They're good listeners. | Nobody does.
a : I know. My mouth's quicker than my sense, #address#. | The best. They don't give advice. | #good.capitalize#. Then we'll get on.

scene ad_first_warm
when topic=season|weather here.season=spring here.outdoors=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : First warm day. #bees.capitalize# came out of #hollow# all at once. | I lay in the grass by #stream# till my back was hot. | The #cold#'s gone. I could shout, but I won't.
b : They'd been waiting. | Sounds lovely. | Shout if you like.
a : All winter. Same as me. | It was. #good.capitalize# as anything. | No. I'll hum. #bees.capitalize# hum.

rule @ad_fly_bark
when concept=bark here.season=summer self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #flies.capitalize#. Off. Off, I said. | #annoyed#. Every fly in the wood's found me.

story ad_gate_beard [topic=memories|animals]
  : Once a swarm came out of #hollow# and hung on the gate like a beard.
  : Everyone ran. I stood still, like I'd been told, and they went past me humming.
  ask : Would you have stood still?
  b : I'd have run. Were you scared?
  b[stage=young] : I'd have run all the way home!
  : Scared stiff. That's why I stood still. #oath#.

dlg @2 resident.hub : #greet#. What's wanted? I've chores. | #greet#, #address#. Quick, then.
